WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
- [Reporter] The Russian
invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:07.850
- Momentum is building for a
war between Ukraine and Russia.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.740
- [Reporter] Tensions
between Russia and the West

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:10.640
are growing rapidly.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.360
- [Reporter] President
Biden considering deploying

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.360
thousands of troops to Eastern Europe.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:16.640
- There are now 100,000 troops

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.853
on the Eastern border of Ukraine.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:24.040
Russia is setting up field
hospitals on this border.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.910
Like this is what preparation
for war looks like.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.410
A legitimate war.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.720
- Ukrainian troops are
watching and waiting,

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.920
saying they are preparing for a fight.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.490
- The U.S. has ordered the
families of embassy staff

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:37.800
to leave Ukraine.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.850
Britain has sent all of their
non-essential staff home.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.270
And now the U.S. is sending
tons of weapons and munitions

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:46.860
to Ukraine's army.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.370
And we're even considering deploying

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.070
our own troops to the region.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.610
I mean, this thing is heating up.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.450
Meanwhile, Russia and the
West have been in Geneva

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.560
and Brussels trying to talk it out,

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.190
and sort of getting nowhere.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.480
- The message is very clear.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.580
Should Russia take
further aggressive actions

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:07.850
against Ukraine the costs will be severe

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.950
and the consequences serious.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:14.010
- It's a scary, grim momentum
that is unpredictable.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:16.160
And the chances of miscalculation

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.000
and escalation are growing.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.460
I want to explain what's going on here,

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.020
but I want to show you
that this isn't just

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.470
typical geopolitical behavior.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.980
Stuff that can just be
explained on the map.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.780
Instead, to understand why
100,000 troops are camped out

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.070
on Ukraine's Eastern
border, ready for war,

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.830
you have to understand Russia

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.270
and how it's been cut down over the ages

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:42.760
from the Slavic empire that
dominated this whole region

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.260
to then the Soviet Union,

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:45.970
which was defeated in the nineties.

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.490
And what you really
have to understand here

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.010
is how that history is transposed

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.610
onto the brain of one man.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.420
This guy, Vladimir Putin.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:58.000
This is a story about regional domination

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.100
and struggles between big powers,

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.960
but really it's the story about

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.690
what Vladimir Putin really wants.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.190
- [Reporter] Russian troops moving swiftly

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:08.519
to take control of
military bases in Crimea.

00:02:08.519 --> 00:02:10.909
- [Reporter] Russia has amassed
more than 100,000 troops

00:02:10.909 --> 00:02:12.470
and a lot of military hardware

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:14.295
at the border with Ukraine.

00:02:14.295 --> 00:02:17.045
(dramatic music)

