00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:59.470
Let's dive back in.

00:03:59.470 --> 00:04:01.660
Okay. Let's get up to speed
on what's happening here.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:04.400
And I'm just going to quickly
give you the highlight version

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.950
of like the news that's happening,

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.840
because I want to get into the juicy part,

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:10.470
which is like why, the
roots of all of this.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.303
So let's go.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.880
A few months ago, Russia started sending

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.240
more and more troops to this border.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.040
It's this massive border
between Ukraine and Russia.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.380
They said they were doing
a military exercise,

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.957
but the rest of the world was like,

00:04:23.957 --> 00:04:27.610
"Yeah, we totally believe
you Russia. Pshaw."

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.110
This was right before this big meeting

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.390
where North American
and European countries

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.880
were coming together to talk about a lot

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.560
of different things, like
these countries often do

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:37.940
in these diplomatic summits.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.780
But soon, because of
Russia's aggressive behavior

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.530
coming in and setting up 100,000 troops

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:45.490
on the border with Ukraine,

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:49.330
the entire summit turned
into a whole, "W-T-F Russia,

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.030
what are you doing on the
border of Ukraine," meeting.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.677
Before the meeting Putin
comes out and says,

00:04:54.677 --> 00:04:57.810
"Listen, I have some
demands for the West."

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:01.840
And everyone's like, "Okay,
Russia, what are your demands?

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:03.860
You know, we have like,
COVID-19 right now.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.090
And like, that's like surging.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.080
So like, we don't need your like,

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.119
bluster about what your demands are."

00:05:09.119 --> 00:05:11.619
And Putin's like, "No,
here's my list of demands."

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.790
Putin's demands for the summit were this:

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.220
number one, that NATO, which
is this big military alliance

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:22.970
between U.S., Canada, and
Europe stop expanding,

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.173
meaning they don't let
any new members in, okay.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:30.050
So, Russia is like, "No more
new members to your, like,

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.720
cool military club that I don't like.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.500
You can't have any more members."

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:38.750
Number two, that NATO
withdraw all of their troops

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.700
from anywhere in Eastern Europe.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:41.587
Basically Putin is saying,

00:05:41.587 --> 00:05:45.350
"I can veto any military cooperation

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:47.760
or troops going between countries

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.290
that have to do with Eastern Europe,

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.470
the place that used to
be the Soviet Union."

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:55.340
Okay, and number three, Putin
demands that America vow

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:58.340
not to protect its
allies in Eastern Europe

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.687
with nuclear weapons.

00:05:59.687 --> 00:06:02.477
"L-O-L," said all of the other countries,

00:06:02.477 --> 00:06:05.060
"You're literally nuts, Vladimir Putin.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.920
Like these are the most
ridiculous demands, ever."

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:10.110
But there he is, Putin,
with these demands.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:12.940
These very, very aggressive demands.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:15.890
And he sort of is implying
that if his demands aren't met,

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.860
he's going to invade Ukraine.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:19.150
I mean, it doesn't work like this.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.030
This is not how
international relations work.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.507
You don't just show up and say like,

00:06:22.507 --> 00:06:25.060
"I'm not gonna allow other
countries to join your alliance

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:26.540
because it makes me feel uncomfortable."

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:28.350
But what I love about this list of demands

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.310
from Vladimir Putin for this summit

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:32.270
is that it gives us a clue

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.730
on what Vladimir Putin really wants.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:36.060
What he's after here.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:39.670
You read them closely and
you can grasp his intentions.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:40.840
But to grasp those intentions

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:43.280
you have to understand what NATO is.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.190
and what Russia and Ukraine used to be.

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:48.270
(dramatic music)

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.860
Okay, so a while back I made this video

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.700
about why Russia is so damn big,

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:56.290
where I explain how modern day
Russia started here in Kiev,

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.620
which is actually modern day Ukraine.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.580
In other words, modern
day Russia, as we know it,

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.470
has its original roots in Ukraine.

00:07:04.470 --> 00:07:06.830
These places grew up together

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.380
and they eventually became a part

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:12.140
of the same mega empire
called the Soviet Union.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.520
They were deeply intertwined,

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.330
not just in their history
and their culture,

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.550
but also in their economy
and their politics.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:20.630
So it's after World War II,

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:24.480
it's like the '50s, '60s,
'70s, and NATO was formed,

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.780
the North Atlantic Treaty Organization.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:30.180
This was a military alliance
between all of these countries,

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:33.160
that was meant to sort
of deter the Soviet Union

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.360
from expanding and taking over the world.

00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:38.570
But as we all know, the Soviet Union,

00:07:38.570 --> 00:07:40.950
which was Russia and all
of these other countries,

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.850
collapsed in 1991.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.760
And all of these Soviet republics,

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.710
including Ukraine, became independent,

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:49.200
meaning they were not now a part

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.850
of one big block of countries anymore.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.920
But just because the
border's all split up,

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.130
it doesn't mean that these
cultural ties actually broke.

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:59.680
Like for example, the
Soviet leader at the time

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.460
of the collapse of the Soviet
Union, this guy, Gorbachev,

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:07.050
he was the son of a Ukrainian
mother and a Russian father.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:09.240
Like he grew up with
his mother singing him

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.110
Ukrainian folk songs.

00:08:11.110 --> 00:08:14.920
In his mind, Ukraine and
Russia were like one thing.

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:18.620
So there was a major
reluctance to accept Ukraine

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:20.790
as a separate thing from Russia.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.340
In so many ways, they are one.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.400
There was another Russian at the time

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.980
who did not accept this new division.

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:29.930
This young intelligence
officer, Vladimir Putin,

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:32.220
who was starting to rise up in the ranks

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:34.340
of post-Soviet Russia.

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:37.360
There's this amazing quote from 2005

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:40.400
where Putin is giving this
state-of-the-union-like address,

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:44.490
where Putin declares the
collapse of the Soviet Union,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:48.890
quote, "The greatest
catastrophe of the 20th century.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:52.110
And as for the Russian people,
it became a genuine tragedy.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:55.810
Tens of millions of fellow
citizens and countrymen

00:08:55.810 --> 00:09:00.150
found themselves beyond the
fringes of Russian territory."

00:09:00.150 --> 00:09:01.420
Do you see how he frames this?

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:04.870
The Soviet Union were all
one people in his mind.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:06.910
And after it collapsed,
all of these people

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:09.970
who are a part of the
motherland were now outside

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:12.850
of the fringes or the
boundaries of Russian territory.

00:09:12.850 --> 00:09:14.123
First off, fact check.

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:17.250
Greatest catastrophe of the 20th century?

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.230
Like, do you remember what else happened

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:20.825
in the 20th century, Vladimir?

00:09:20.825 --> 00:09:23.492
(ominous music)

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:29.840
Putin's worry about the
collapse of this one people

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.370
starts to get way worse
when the West, his enemy,

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:35.220
starts showing up to his neighborhood

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.620
to all these ex-Soviet countries
that are now independent.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:40.590
The West starts selling their ideology

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:43.750
of democracy and capitalism
and inviting them

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:47.280
to join their military
alliance called NATO.

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.600
And guess what?

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.090
These countries are totally buying it.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:55.430
All these ex-Soviet countries
are now joining NATO.

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:57.150
And some of them, the EU.

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.750
And Putin is hating this.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:03.020
He's like not only did
the Soviet Union divide

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:04.750
and all of these people are now outside

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:06.360
of the Russia motherland,

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:09.560
but now they're being
persuaded by the West

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:11.500
to join their military alliance.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.130
This is terrible news.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.240
Over the years, this continues to happen,

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:18.540
while Putin himself starts to chip away

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:22.230
at Russian institutions,
making them weaker and weaker.

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:23.940
He's silencing his rivals

00:10:23.940 --> 00:10:26.901
and he's consolidating power in himself.

00:10:26.901 --> 00:10:29.818
(triumphant music)

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.170
And in the past few years,

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:35.350
he's effectively silenced
anyone who can challenge him;

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:37.170
any institution, any court,

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:39.943
or any political rival
have all been silenced.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:44.600
It's been decades since
the Soviet Union fell,

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.440
but as Putin gains more power,

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:49.230
he still sees the region through the lens

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:54.230
of the old Cold War,
Soviet, Slavic empire view.

00:10:55.430 --> 00:10:58.040
He sees this region as one big block

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:00.727
that has been torn
apart by outside forces.

00:11:00.727 --> 00:11:03.980
"The greatest catastrophe
of the 20th century."

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:05.700
And the worst situation of all of these,

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:08.180
according to Putin, is Ukraine,

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:10.790
which was like the gem
of the Soviet Union.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.960
There was tons of cultural heritage.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:15.920
Again, Russia sort of started in Ukraine,

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.200
not to mention it was a very populous

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:21.560
and industrious, resource-rich place.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:25.470
And over the years Ukraine
has been drifting west.

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:27.500
It hasn't joined NATO
yet, but more and more,

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:31.360
it's been electing pro-Western presidents.

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.150
It's been flirting with
membership in NATO.

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:35.860
It's becoming less and less attached

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:39.420
to the Russian heritage
that Putin so adores.

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.070
And more than half of Ukrainians say

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:44.360
that they'd be down to join the EU.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:48.050
64% of them say that it
would be cool joining NATO.

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:51.880
But Putin can't handle
this. He is in total denial.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.680
Like an ex-boyfriend who
handle his ex-girlfriend

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.210
starting to date someone else,

00:11:56.210 --> 00:11:59.090
Putin can't let Ukraine go.

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:00.160
He won't let go.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:01.060
So for the past decade,

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:02.980
he's been trying to keep the West out

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:06.470
and bring Ukraine back into
the motherland of Russia.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:09.240
This usually takes the
form of Putin sending

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.320
secret soldiers from Russia into Ukraine

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:16.100
to help the people in Ukraine
who want to like separate

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:17.610
from Ukraine and join Russia.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.890
It also takes the form of, oh yeah,

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:23.200
stealing entire parts
of Ukraine for Russia.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.210
- Russian troops moving
swiftly to take control

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:26.870
of military bases in Crimea.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.710
- Like in 2014, Putin just did this.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:30.260
- To what America is officially calling

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.910
a Russian invasion of Ukraine.

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.980
- He went down and just
snatched this bit of Ukraine

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.120
and folded it into Russia.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:40.160
So you're starting to
see what's going on here.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.610
Putin's life's work is
to salvage what he calls

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:47.100
the greatest catastrophe
of the 20th century,

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:49.960
the division and the separation

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:52.080
of the Soviet republics from Russia.

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:55.120
So let's get to present day. It's 2022.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:57.280
Putin is at it again.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.370
And honestly, if you
really want to understand

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.630
the mind of Vladimir Putin
and his whole view on this,

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:05.177
you have to read this.

00:13:05.177 --> 00:13:09.600
"On the History of Unity of
Russians and Ukrainians,"

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:11.230
by Vladimir Putin.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.330
A blog post that kind of sounds

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.510
like a ninth grade history essay.

00:13:15.510 --> 00:13:18.870
In this essay, Vladimir Putin argues

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:22.190
that Russia and Ukraine are one people.

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:25.730
He calls them essentially
the same historical

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:27.710
and spiritual space.

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:29.790
Kind of beautiful writing, honestly.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.130
Anyway, he argues that the division

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:35.307
between the two countries is due to quote,

00:13:35.307 --> 00:13:38.310
"a deliberate effort by those forces

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:41.470
that have always sought
to undermine our unity."

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:44.530
And that the formula they
use, these outside forces,

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.720
is a classic one: divide and rule.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:51.250
And then he launches
into this super in-depth,

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:56.250
like 10-page argument, as to
every single historical beat

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.610
of Ukraine and Russia's history

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.050
to make this argument that like,

00:14:01.050 --> 00:14:04.190
this is one people and the
division is totally because

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:07.320
of outside powers, i.e. the West.

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:08.960
Okay, but listen, there's this moment

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:10.580
at the end of the post,

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:13.300
that actually kind of hit me in a big way.

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:16.820
He says this, "Just have a
look at Austria and Germany,

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:21.030
or the U.S. and Canada, how
they live next to each other.

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:23.610
Close in ethnic composition, culture,

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.940
and in fact, sharing one language,

00:14:25.940 --> 00:14:28.450
they remain sovereign states
with their own interests,

00:14:28.450 --> 00:14:30.000
with their own foreign policy.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.500
But this does not prevent them

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:35.370
from the closest integration
or allied relations.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:38.740
They have very conditional,
transparent borders.

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:42.700
And when crossing them
citizens feel at home.

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:47.350
They create families,
study, work, do business.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:51.210
Incidentally, so do millions
of those born in Ukraine

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:52.530
who now live in Russia.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.807
We see them as our own close people."

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:00.190
I mean, listen, like,

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.260
I'm not in support of what Putin is doing,

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:05.880
but like that, it's like a
pretty solid like analogy.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.000
If China suddenly showed
up and started like

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:13.640
coaxing Canada into being
a part of its alliance,

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.870
I would be a little bit
like, "What's going on here?"

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:18.110
That's what Putin feels.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:20.300
And so I kind of get what he means there.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:24.400
There's a deep heritage and
connection between these people.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:27.650
And he's seen that falter and dissolve

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.070
and he doesn't like it.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.360
He clearly genuinely feels a brotherhood

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.520
and this deep heritage connection

00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:37.413
with the people of Ukraine.

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:42.180
Okay, okay, okay, okay. Putin, I get it.

00:15:42.180 --> 00:15:44.160
Your essay is compelling there at the end.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.030
You're clearly very smart and well-read.

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:50.610
But this does not justify
what you've been up to. Okay?

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:53.840
It doesn't justify sending
100,000 troops to the border

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.500
or sending cyber soldiers to sabotage

00:15:56.500 --> 00:16:00.010
the Ukrainian government,
or annexing territory,

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:01.950
fueling a conflict that has killed

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:04.470
tens of thousands of
people in Eastern Ukraine.

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:06.100
No. Okay.

00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:08.840
No matter how much affection
you feel for Ukrainian heritage

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:12.130
and its connection to
Russia, this is not okay.

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:13.700
Again, it's like the boyfriend

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.280
who genuinely loves his girlfriend.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.730
They had a great relationship,

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:20.990
but they broke up and she's
free to see whomever she wants.

00:16:20.990 --> 00:16:22.847
But Putin is not ready to let go.

00:16:22.847 --> 00:16:24.470
- [Man In Blue Shirt] What
the hell's wrong with you?

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:25.830
I love you, Jessica.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.210
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:16:27.210 --> 00:16:29.223
Dude, don't fucking touch me.

00:16:29.223 --> 00:16:31.140
I love you.
- Worldstar!

00:16:32.211 --> 00:16:33.750
- What is wrong with you?
- Just stop!

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:37.880
- Putin has constructed
his own reality here.

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:40.990
One in which Ukraine is
actually being controlled

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:43.610
by shadowy Western forces

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:46.360
who are holding the
people of Ukraine hostage.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:49.450
And if that he invades,
it will be a swift victory

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:53.280
because Ukrainians will
accept him with open arms.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.657
The great liberator.

00:16:54.657 --> 00:16:57.574
(triumphant music)

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.830
Like, this guy's a total romantic.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:02.820
He's a history buff and a romantic.

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:04.570
And he has a hill to die on here.

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:06.430
And it is liberating the people

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:08.890
who have been taken from
the Russian motherland.

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:10.477
Kind of like the abusive
boyfriend, who's like,

00:17:10.477 --> 00:17:12.170
"She actually really loves me,

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:13.810
but it's her annoying friends

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:16.000
who were planting all
these ideas in her head.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.360
That's why she broke up with me."

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:20.117
And it's like, "No, dude, she's over you."

00:17:20.117 --> 00:17:21.760
- [Man In Blue Shirt] What
the hell is wrong with you?

00:17:21.760 --> 00:17:22.593
I love you, Jessica.

00:17:22.593 --> 00:17:23.980
- I mean, maybe this
video should be called

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:27.192
Putin is just like your
abusive ex-boyfriend.

00:17:27.192 --> 00:17:28.666
- [Man In Blue Shirt] What
the hell is wrong with you?

00:17:28.666 --> 00:17:29.685
I love you, Jessica!

00:17:29.685 --> 00:17:32.650
- Worldstar!
- What's wrong with you?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.750
- Okay. So where does this leave us?

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:39.750
It's 2022, Putin is showing
up to these meetings in Europe

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:41.970
to tell them where he stands.

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:45.790
He says, "NATO, you cannot
expand anymore. No new members.

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:47.520
And you need to withdraw all your troops

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.940
from Eastern Europe, my neighborhood."

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.980
He knows these demands
will never be accepted

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:53.130
because they're ludicrous.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:57.217
But what he's doing is
showing a false effort to say,

00:17:57.217 --> 00:17:59.350
"Well, we tried to
negotiate with the West,

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.560
but they didn't want to."

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:02.590
Hence giving a little
bit more justification

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:04.210
to a Russian invasion.

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:07.440
So will Russia invade?
Is there war coming?

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.140
Maybe; it's impossible to know

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:11.470
because it's all inside
of the head of this guy.

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:13.470
But, if I were to make the best argument

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:16.800
that war is not coming tomorrow,

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:18.240
I would look at a few things.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:21.500
Number one, war in Ukraine
would be incredibly costly

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.780
for Vladimir Putin.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:25.420
Russia has a far superior
army to Ukraine's,

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:27.560
but still, Ukraine has a very good army

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:29.040
that is supported by the West

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.940
and would give Putin a
pretty bad bloody nose

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.080
in any invasion.

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:35.560
Controlling territory in
Ukraine would be very hard.

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:37.650
Ukraine is a giant country.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:39.560
They would fight back
and it would be very hard

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:42.050
to actually conquer and
take over territory.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:45.930
Another major point here is
that if Russia invades Ukraine,

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.440
this gives NATO new purpose.

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:51.870
If you remember, NATO was
created because of the Cold War,

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.450
because the Soviet Union
was big and nuclear powered.

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.550
Once the Soviet Union fell,

00:18:56.550 --> 00:18:58.990
NATO sort of has been
looking for a new purpose

00:18:58.990 --> 00:19:00.520
over the past couple of decades.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:02.090
If Russia invades Ukraine,

00:19:02.090 --> 00:19:05.700
NATO suddenly has a brand
new purpose to unite

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:09.050
and to invest in becoming
more powerful than ever.

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:09.900
Putin knows that.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.090
And it would be very bad news
for him if that happened.

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:15.040
But most importantly,
perhaps the easiest clue

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.250
for me to believe that
war isn't coming tomorrow

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:20.030
is the Russian propaganda machine

00:19:20.030 --> 00:19:23.210
is not preparing the Russian
people for an invasion.

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:25.620
In 2014, when Russia was about to invade

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.000
and take over Crimea,
this part of Ukraine,

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.820
there was a barrage of state propaganda

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.660
that prepared the Russian people

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:36.270
that this was a justified attack.

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.330
So when it happened, it wasn't a surprise

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:39.750
and it felt very normal.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:42.130
That isn't happening right now in Russia.

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:45.210
At least for now. It may
start happening tomorrow.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:49.430
But for now, I think Putin
is showing up to the border,

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:53.270
flexing his muscles and showing
the West that he is earnest.

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:55.530
I'm not sure that he's
going to invade tomorrow,

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:57.100
but he very well could.

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:59.270
I mean, read the guy's blog post

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:02.570
and you'll realize that he
is a romantic about this.

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:05.950
He is incredibly idealistic
about the glory days

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:10.370
of the Slavic empires, and
he wants to get it back.

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.520
So there is dangerous
momentum towards war.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:18.070
And the way war works is even
a small little, like, fight,

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.130
can turn into the other guy

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.230
doing something bigger and crazier.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:23.640
And then the other person has to respond

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:24.880
with something a little bit bigger.

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:26.510
That's called escalation.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:28.010
And there's not really a ceiling

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:31.750
to how much that momentum
can spin out of control.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.720
That is why it's so scary
when two nuclear countries

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:35.600
go to war with each other,

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:37.510
because there's kind of no ceiling.

00:20:37.510 --> 00:20:40.790
So yeah, it's dangerous. This is scary.

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:42.300
I'm not sure what happens next here,

00:20:42.300 --> 00:20:44.800
but the best we can do
is keep an eye on this.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:48.040
At least for now, we better understand

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:51.360
what Putin really wants
out of all of this.

